Richard Curnow wrote:

> In chapter 3 of the Ref. Grammar, there is a statement
> 
>    In Lojban, doubled consonants are excluded altogether, and clusters
>    are limited to two or three members, except in Lojbanized names.

"Members" = "consonants", but excludes syllabic consonants.  3.4 and
3.6 should be corrected to this effect.

>    cidjrspageti
> 
> which contain clusters of 4 consonants,

Actually 5 consonants.  But the syllabication is "cidj,r,spageti",
so there are never more than two non-syllabic consonants in a row.

